SPRD SIPC: read the raw task state through the Linux 6.6 task_struct member.

These two sites only print diagnostic task state as %lx. READ_ONCE protects the
concurrent state read, and the unsigned long cast preserves the format contract
for the unsigned int __state member. Existing linux/kernel.h supplies READ_ONCE.
No scheduling behavior or kernel Kconfig symbols are changed.

Reference:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.6/include/linux/sched.h

--- a/package/mtk/applications/5g-modem/quectel_SRPD_PCIE/src/sipc/sbuf.c
+++ b/package/mtk/applications/5g-modem/quectel_SRPD_PCIE/src/sipc/sbuf.c
@@ -1485,7 +1485,7 @@
 					 "%s %d: %s, state=0x%lx, pid=%d.\n",
 					 phead,
 					 cnt, task->comm,
-					 task->state, task->pid);
+					 (unsigned long)READ_ONCE(task->__state), task->pid);
 				cnt++;
 				len = strlen(status_info);
 			}
@@ -1569,7 +1569,7 @@
 				   cnt);
 			seq_printf(m, ": %s, state = 0x%lx, pid = %d\n",
 				   task->comm,
-				   task->state,
+				   (unsigned long)READ_ONCE(task->__state),
 				   task->pid);
 			cnt++;
 		}
